    "termsOfUse": "The standard Data Transfer Agreement (DTA) used at the Erasmus MC must be signed without adjustments. This DTA template has been set up in conjunction with legal advisors of all Dutch academic hospitals and serves to facilitate and regulate the transfer of/access to personal data that were previously collected by a Dutch University hospital (“Provider”) from patients, participants and/or volunteers for the purpose of scientific research, by an external not-for-profit party (“Recipient”).\nData Transfer Agreement: https://elsi.health-ri.nl/sites/elsi/files/2020-07/20.30815%20OenO%20Template%20-%20Data%20Sharing%20Agreement.pdf",
    "confidentialityDeclaration": "No",
    "specialPermissions": "Access to the data can be requested through contacting the project coordinator via projectvaluecare@erasmusmc.nl. A form will be provided which the requestor has to complete and send back. The requestor needs to provide the following information: \n► Study team (description) \n►  Study short introduction \n►  Research questions \n►  Brief methods definition \n►  Requested data \n► Ethical approval (obtained or not needed) \n► Legal basis for processing \n► How the party(parties) intend to respect the users’ rights. \n\nOnce received, the scientific committee of the ValueCare project will evaluate the request. \nIf approved, a Data Transfer Agreement (DTA) in line with GDPR regulations and/or a Collaboration Agreement will be created and should be signed before data is shared. Only data requests in line with the Terms of Use will be taken into consideration.\n\nOnce signed, the data will be transferred in a secure way, e.g. through Surf Filesender.",
    "restrictions": "See Data Transfer Agreement",
